{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1207925-language-merit-question","id":1207925,"title":"Language Merit Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-17T04:02:14-07:00","id":1207925,"title":"Language Merit Question","content":"If you possess five Language Merits or more, then you\u2019ve<br /> begun to understand the principles of language itself and can<br /> try to unravel languages you don\u2019t already know (Intelligence<br /> + Enigmas, difficulty 7 or higher).<br /> <br /> Does this mean with a simple roll of intelligence and enigmas, a mage and learn garou? After only five minutes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T04:12:07-07:00","id":1207927,"title":"","content":"I think it's accurate to say that you won't immediately understand the language, no. Not at all.<br /> But you are probably able to quickly deduct how its grammatical structure and syntax works, differentiate between articles, object and names, and be able to learn a language much, much quicker, especially if it is written down,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T07:55:53-07:00","id":1207984,"title":"","content":"To learn a language in five minutes, I think you'd need Time magic or Mind. Mind 3 is basically a universal translator.<br /> <br /> I'd make the time to pick up a new language using Intelligence and Enigmas based on how close the language is to other languages the mage knows. For example, I took German in high school and remember a little. I've studied Latin American history and know a few Spanish words. I have never studied Chinese, and my exposure to it is pretty much in RPGs. I'm going to have a lot easier time figuring out German or a similar language than I am Chinese and figuring out the syntax will be a lot faster when there is experience. I did have to take my qualifying language test twice because I forgot how significant the subjunctive (if-then) case was in German historical writing. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T14:19:00-07:00","id":1208173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thkaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1207925-language-merit-question#post1207925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this mean with a simple roll of intelligence and enigmas, a mage and learn garou? After only five minutes?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It means that they get a chance to roll to see if they understand what's being said. There's a huge difference between being able to roll to catch part of a conversation, and actually knowing a language. I don't speak Spanish. But between studying other Romance languages, and cultural assimilation, I might be able to figure out what two people speaking Spanish are saying (esp. written where I can see the words and the roots).<br /> <br /> Perception (not necessarily the Attribute) is also important here. A character can't unravel what they can't perceive. Garou Tongue as the example, involves a lot of communications that aren't in the normal human range of perceptions, so without using some (albeit simply) Life magic it could be impossible to get to roll simply because so much is going on you're not sensing. Similarly you can't roll just because someone tells you a language exists. You need examples to start on. &quot;Akkadian is a thing,&quot; doesn't let you figure out Akkadian, you need some artifacts of Akkadian to start to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T14:47:43-07:00","id":1208189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thkaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1207925-language-merit-question#post1207925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this mean with a simple roll of intelligence and enigmas, a mage and learn garou? After only five minutes?</div> </div> </div> </div>They may potentially be able to decypher garou glyphs given examination, but they would have to do this each time and context matters. Could they say understand what's spoken? no","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T06:28:22-07:00","id":1208417,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that a simple workaround for all language is Mind 3. Alternatively, Spirit is a good way of getting translation done, although keeping a positive relationship with a polyglot ghost might be a bit demanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T07:44:27-07:00","id":1208436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1207925-language-merit-question?p=1208417#post1208417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that a simple workaround for all language is Mind 3. Alternatively, Spirit is a good way of getting translation done, although keeping a positive relationship with a polyglot ghost might be a bit demanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also contract the services of a non-ghost Spirit of languages. The Astral Umbra is bound to be full of them. Of course, that doesn't make such a pact any less costly. A language spirit would probably mandate the character actively learn other languages (rendering the contract pointless in the long term) or even to teach languages to other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T09:28:27-07:00","id":1208475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1207925-language-merit-question?p=1208436#post1208436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also contract the services of a non-ghost Spirit of languages. The Astral Umbra is bound to be full of them. Of course, that doesn't make such a pact any less costly. A language spirit would probably mandate the character actively learn other languages (rendering the contract pointless in the long term) or even to teach languages to other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts are more malleable IMO. Get a'hold of their fetter and do them a few favours and they're a reliable retainer in some regards (sentry, lessons).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T14:23:47-07:00","id":1210597,"title":"","content":"Language merit is what Daniel has in stargate. He is able to make links between known and unkown words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T19:06:44-07:00","id":1210743,"title":"","content":"Well, he has as a more defining feature the Natural Linguist Merit (more languages, and a bonus to speaking languages in other cultures). Stargate (at least in the movie) doesn't really apply because Daniel is dealing with reconciling the modern recreation of a 'dead' language with a living dialect of it that was never lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T19:03:05-07:00","id":1464448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1207925-language-merit-question?p=1208417#post1208417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that a simple workaround for all language is Mind 3. Alternatively, Spirit is a good way of getting translation done, although keeping a positive relationship with a polyglot ghost might be a bit demanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good for yourself, but what if you have a friend who doesn't have mind 3 or a mortal minion and you need them to know a language to do a job for you? Can you download a language into their brain with Mind 4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T19:49:29-07:00","id":1464454,"title":"","content":"While the rules aren't always consistent about what dot level might be required? Yes, unless something about a specific effect says otherwise you can cast it on someone else so they can benefit instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T03:59:29-07:00","id":1464494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1207925-language-merit-question?p=1464454#post1464454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the rules aren't always consistent about what dot level might be required? Yes, unless something about a specific effect says otherwise you can cast it on someone else so they can benefit instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I said Mind 4, because usually you need one more dot to effect someone else compared to effecting yourself.<br /> <br /> Of course, I was assuming you had to know the language in question to give it to someone. I wasn't thinking of giving them a mental universal translator. That would seem too much to give a non magical person, but maybe I'm being limited by my own paradigm. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T11:23:33-07:00","id":1464525,"title":"","content":"Well, it would probably be vulgar if you cast it on a Sleeper (like most perception magic), but considering how well real-time translation software is developing, it wouldn't be hard for a technomage to do as long as it sticks to human languages. IRL, you can buy good real-time translator apps for a smartphone that (depending on price and Internet connectivity) can facilitate conversations between people without any mutual language knowledge with 90-95% accuracy in the most common 20-40 languages in the world.<br /> <br /> We're nowhere near &quot;universal&quot; translators that can try to linguistically analyze a language and start translating it in real time, but we're not far from, say, Babylon 5 where there's a language that's specifically designed to be extremely easy to translate with computer assistance, and first contact situations are usually handled by sending out a message in that language with instructions for compiling a program that can use it as the base for a real-time translator under the assumption that any space-faring species is going to be advanced enough to figure it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}